### Dealer Kavach - VS Code REST Client collection
### Install: REST Client (humao.rest-client) extension.
### Run requests top-to-bottom; @token / @dealerId / @dsId / @runId are
### populated automatically from prior responses.

@host = http://localhost:4000
@base = {{host}}/api/v1
@adminEmail = admin@dealerkavach.local
@adminPassword = Admin@12345

### The TT Density block (18-34) needs three things this file cannot invent: a
### dealer that already has the service attached, that dealer's own app login, and
### a photo saved next to this file as `register-page.jpg`. Fill these in first.
### @ttDate must be today or one of the six days before it, IST.
@ttDealerId = 000000000000000000000000
@ttDate = 2026-08-24
@dealerEmail = owner@example.com
@dealerPassword = ChangeMe@12345

### The slip block (35-40) is the whole of Phase 2: an admin can run it every
### morning for a week and see what the paper reads, with no screen and no box
### ever touched. It needs a HAND-TYPED outlet - a dealer whose IRAS Shift Data
### service is not ACTIVE, whose day has already been opened (request 41), and
### whose DSR layout lists the nozzles - plus a photo saved next to this file as
### `shift-slip.jpg`. SLIP_READ_ENABLED must be true on the server.
@slipDealerId = 000000000000000000000000
@slipDate = 2026-09-02
@slipShiftTime = 06:30

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### 1. Login (captures token)
# @name login
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### 2. Who am I
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. List plugin catalog
GET {{base}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. List dealers
GET {{base}}/dealers?page=1&pageSize=20&sort=createdAt:desc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Create a new dealer (stage 1)
# @name createDealer
POST {{base}}/dealers
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "REST Demo Petrol",
  "ownerContact": {
    "name": "Demo Owner",
    "phone": "+91-9000000000",
    "email": "demo.owner@example.com"
  },
  "pumpLocation": {
    "address": "12 MG Road, Bengaluru",
    "city": "Bengaluru",
    "state": "KA",
    "pincode": "560001",
    "lat": 12.97,
    "lng": 77.59
  },
  "gst": "29AAACR5055K1Z7",
  "pan": "AAACR5055K"
}

@dealerId = {{createDealer.response.body.data.id}}

### 6. Complete stage 2 (auto-promotes to ACTIVE)
PATCH {{base}}/dealers/{{dealerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bankDetails": {
    "accountHolder": "REST Demo Petrol",
    "accountNumber": "123456789012",
    "ifsc": "HDFC0000123",
    "bankName": "HDFC Bank",
    "branch": "MG Road"
  },
  "complianceDocs": [
    { "label": "GST Certificate", "url": "https://example.com/gst.pdf" },
    { "label": "PAN Card", "url": "https://example.com/pan.pdf" }
  ],
  "slaTier": "SILVER"
}

### 7. Audit log for the new dealer
GET {{base}}/dealers/{{dealerId}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 8. Attach the custom-request plugin
# @name attachService
POST {{base}}/dealers/{{dealerId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "serviceId": "custom-request",
  "config": {
    "requestType": "manual-audit",
    "payload": { "ticketId": "T-1001" }
  }
}

@dsId = {{attachService.response.body.data.id}}

### 9. List attached services for the dealer
GET {{base}}/dealers/{{dealerId}}/services
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Run the attached service now
# @name runNow
POST {{base}}/dealer-services/{{dsId}}/run-now
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

@runId = {{runNow.response.body.data.runId}}

### 11. Look up the run we just created
GET {{base}}/runs/{{runId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. List recent runs (filtered to this dealer)
GET {{base}}/runs?dealerId={{dealerId}}&page=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 13. Pause the attached service
PATCH {{base}}/dealer-services/{{dsId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PAUSED"
}

### 14. Re-activate it
PATCH {{base}}/dealer-services/{{dsId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 15. Dashboard overview snapshot
GET {{base}}/overview
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 16. Detach the service
DELETE {{base}}/dealer-services/{{dsId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 17. Delete the demo dealer (cascades dealer-services)
DELETE {{base}}/dealers/{{dealerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 18. TT Density - the dealer's pane payload (headline densities + 14 days)
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 19. TT Density - invoices in a window (captures the newest invoice)
# @name ttInvoices
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/invoices?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31&page=1&pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

@ttInvoiceId = {{ttInvoices.response.body.data.items.0.id}}

### 20. One invoice in full (every product line and its Density@15)
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/invoices/{{ttInvoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 21. Signed URLs for that invoice's PDF
### `viewUrl` is inline (the drawer's iframe), `downloadUrl` is an attachment.
### 404 here means the PDF has not been fetched yet - that is a UI state, not a bug.
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/invoices/{{ttInvoiceId}}/pdf-url
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 22. Register days for one month (what the admin calendar asks for)
### Swap `from`/`to` for `?limit=30` to get "the last 30 days" instead.
### Days with no photo come back too - the gaps are the point.
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/days?from=2026-08-01&to=2026-08-31
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 23. Signed URLs for one day's register photo
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/days/{{ttDate}}/photo-url
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 24. Presign a register photo for that dealer (admin uploading on their behalf)
# @name ttPresign
POST {{base}}/uploads/sign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "register-page.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000,
  "scope": "tt-density",
  "dealerId": "{{ttDealerId}}"
}

@ttUploadUrl = {{ttPresign.response.body.data.uploadUrl}}
@ttStorageKey = {{ttPresign.response.body.data.storageKey}}

### 25. Put the bytes where the presign says (no Authorization - the URL is the credential)
PUT {{ttUploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./register-page.jpg

### 26. Mark the day, on the dealer's behalf
### The response records `uploadedBy.kind = "admin"` and the admin's name, which is
### what the calendar prints. Older than 60 days counting today is refused.
POST {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/days/{{ttDate}}/photo
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storageKey": "{{ttStorageKey}}",
  "filename": "register-page.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000,
  "note": "Sent on WhatsApp, added by MDG"
}

### 27. Fetch this dealer's invoices now (202, then the run happens in the background)
### `lookbackDays` is a one-run override - it does not change the schedule.
POST {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "lookbackDays": 7
}

### 28. Sign in as the dealer (their own app login, not an admin's)
# @name dealerLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{dealerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{dealerPassword}}"
}

@dealerToken = {{dealerLogin.response.body.data.token}}

### 29. What the dealer's own screen sees
### No invoice, no PDF, no rupee figure. `earliestMarkableDate` is today - 6 and is
### what the app feeds to `<input type="date" min>`. A dealer without the service
### gets 200 with `attached: false`, never a 404.
GET {{base}}/tt-density/me
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}

### 30. The dealer marks today (presign with their OWN token, then mark)
# @name dealerPresign
POST {{base}}/uploads/sign
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "register-page.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000,
  "scope": "tt-density",
  "dealerId": "{{ttDealerId}}"
}

@dealerUploadUrl = {{dealerPresign.response.body.data.uploadUrl}}
@dealerStorageKey = {{dealerPresign.response.body.data.storageKey}}

### 31. Put the bytes
PUT {{dealerUploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./register-page.jpg

### 32. Mark the day as the dealer
POST {{base}}/tt-density/me/days/{{ttDate}}/photo
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storageKey": "{{dealerStorageKey}}",
  "filename": "register-page.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000
}

### 33. The dealer reading back their own photo
GET {{base}}/tt-density/me/days/{{ttDate}}/photo-url
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}

### 34. The fence, as a request: a dealer token must not reach an admin route (expect 403)
GET {{base}}/tt-density/dealers/{{ttDealerId}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}

### 35. Open the day by hand, if it is not open yet (201 the first time, 200 after)
POST {{base}}/iras-data/dealers/{{slipDealerId}}/days/{{slipDate}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "shiftTime": "{{slipShiftTime}}"
}

### 36. Presign the slip photo. ADMIN ONLY - a dealer token gets 403 here, and
### the key comes back under `slip/<dealerId>/`, never under `avatars/`.
# @name slipPresign
POST {{base}}/uploads/sign
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "shift-slip.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000,
  "scope": "slip",
  "dealerId": "{{slipDealerId}}"
}

@slipUploadUrl = {{slipPresign.response.body.data.uploadUrl}}
@slipStorageKey = {{slipPresign.response.body.data.storageKey}}

### 37. Put the bytes (no Authorization - the URL is the credential)
PUT {{slipUploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./shift-slip.jpg

### 38. Read the slip. Writes NOTHING to the day - it answers with what the paper
### says, and `reading.readings[].batchable` is true only where both readers
### produced the same digits AND the rupees printed on the same block prove them.
### `quota` says how many of the day's ten reads are left.
# @name slipRead
POST {{base}}/iras-data/dealers/{{slipDealerId}}/days/{{slipDate}}/read-slip
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storageKey": "{{slipStorageKey}}",
  "filename": "shift-slip.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000
}

@slipReadId = {{slipRead.response.body.data.slipReadId}}

### 39. The photograph again, signed inline for 15 minutes
GET {{base}}/iras-data/dealers/{{slipDealerId}}/slip-reads/{{slipReadId}}/photo-url
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 40. The fence, as a request: a key under another dealer's prefix (expect 400,
### "That photo does not belong to this dealer.")
POST {{base}}/iras-data/dealers/{{slipDealerId}}/days/{{slipDate}}/read-slip
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "storageKey": "slip/000000000000000000000001/not-yours.jpg",
  "filename": "shift-slip.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000
}

### ─────────────────────── Document validity (41-50) ───────────────────────
### Papers that run out, and the ladder that chases them. The block needs a
### dealer and that dealer's own app login (reuse @dealerEmail / @dealerPassword
### from the TT block above), plus a file saved beside this one as `fire-noc.jpg`.
@docDealerId = 000000000000000000000000

### 41. The live catalog. `tracksValidity` is what decides whether the accept
### dialog asks for a date at all; a row that has never been edited comes back
### with the shipped ladder resolved rather than an empty one.
GET {{base}}/document-kinds?activeOnly=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 42. Ask a dealer for a paper that runs out. `silent: true` suppresses the
### push, and exists for the admin who ALREADY has the paper and is about to file
### it — without it the dealer's phone asks for a certificate that was on file
### before the buzz finished.
# @name docAsk
POST {{base}}/asks
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "dealerId": "{{docDealerId}}",
  "kindCode": "fire-noc",
  "periodKind": "NONE",
  "periodKey": "",
  "reminderOffsetDays": [30, 7, 1]
}

@docAskId = {{docAsk.response.body.data.id}}

### 43. Presign, as the dealer. An ask's object is filed under
### `ask/<dealerId>/<askId>/`, so the row has to exist before there is anywhere
### to put the file.
# @name docSign
POST {{base}}/uploads/sign
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "filename": "fire-noc.jpg",
  "contentType": "image/jpeg",
  "size": 240000,
  "scope": "ask",
  "dealerId": "{{docDealerId}}",
  "askId": "{{docAskId}}"
}

@docUploadUrl = {{docSign.response.body.data.uploadUrl}}
@docKey = {{docSign.response.body.data.storageKey}}

### 44. Put the bytes (no Authorization - the URL is the credential)
PUT {{docUploadUrl}}
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./fire-noc.jpg

### 45. Send it, as the dealer. `validUntil` here is a COURTESY, not a record:
### whoever accepts confirms or corrects it, and their value is the one that
### governs (ADR 0011 — admin or automation certifies, never the dealer).
POST {{base}}/asks/me/{{docAskId}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attachment": {
    "storageKey": "{{docKey}}",
    "filename": "fire-noc.jpg",
    "contentType": "image/jpeg",
    "size": 240000,
    "kind": "image"
  },
  "validUntil": "2027-03-31",
  "clientRef": "restclient-doc-0001"
}

### 46. Accept it WITHOUT a date (expect 400, "This paper runs out. Enter the date
### printed on it before accepting."). The schema cannot enforce this — it cannot
### see the catalog — so the route does.
POST {{base}}/asks/{{docAskId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 47. Accept it properly. Where the kind names a `profileFieldKey`, this also
### writes the date onto that field on the outlet Info tab, so the two screens
### cannot come to hold rival dates for one licence.
POST {{base}}/asks/{{docAskId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "validUntil": "2027-03-31"
}

### 48. Fix a mistyped date, or quieten this one certificate. `reminderOffsetDays: []`
### means NEVER REMIND about this paper — a real setting, distinct from omitting
### the field, which leaves the kind's ladder in force. `validUntil: null` clears
### the date and the mirrored one. Steps already settled stay settled: a date
### pushed six months out does not re-fire a warning the dealer already had.
PATCH {{base}}/asks/{{docAskId}}/validity
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "validUntil": "2027-06-30"
}

### 49. The dealer's filing cabinet. ACCEPTED papers only, sorted most-urgent
### first, `dealerVisible`-gated in the QUERY. `validityState` and `validityLabel`
### are decided on the SERVER against the server's IST day — a phone whose clock
### is a day fast must never badge a valid licence red.
GET {{base}}/asks/me/on-file
Authorization: Bearer {{dealerToken}}

### 50. The estate register: what is running out, across every dealer. Naming
### either filter switches the sort to `validUntil` ascending — without it every
### paper that carries an expiry is `periodKind: NONE`, sorts last on the empty
### period key, and a full page comes back holding no licences at all.
### `expiringWithinDays` has NO lower bound: a certificate that lapsed last month
### is more urgent than one lapsing next week.
GET {{base}}/asks?expiringWithinDays=30
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 51. Edit the ladder for a whole KIND (super-admin). This is the cadence
### editor's route. An empty array here silences the kind for every dealer.
PATCH {{base}}/super-admin/document-kinds/fire-noc
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reminderOffsetDays": [45, 15, 3, 1]
}

